IMPORT prelude

-- Long Service Leave Act 2018 (Vic) -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- It uses only the built-in date functions (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH,
-- DATE_YEAR), not the daydate library. The Act counts in years ("7 years of continuous employment", s 6; "within 6 years
-- after the employee's entitlement to the money arises", s 26(4); "at least 7 years after the employee stops working",
-- s 37(3)), in weeks ("within 12 weeks after", ss 11(5), (7), 12(6); "within 52 weeks after", ss 12(6)(c), 13(2); "at
-- least 12 weeks' written notice", s 19(1)) and in days ("at least 7 days before", s 50(1)).
--
-- A period of years after a day ends on the same day of the month that many years later; where that month has no such
-- day (29 February in a common year), on the last day of that month (fork F1). A week is 7 days.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Long Service
-- Leave Act 2018, Version No. 006 (12 December 2025), not the authorised version. (c) State of Victoria; published with
-- the authority of the Government Printer for the State of Victoria. No part may be reproduced except in accordance with
-- the Copyright Act 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Long Service Leave Act 2018`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

-- Plain days from one day to another (negative if the second is earlier).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the start` `to` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

-- The day a given number of plain days after a day.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `days after` `the start` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the start` PLUS n)

-- Whether the first day is earlier than the second.
GIVEN `the first` IS A DATE, `the second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day` `the first` `is before` `the second` IF
    DATE_SERIAL `the first` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second`

-- Whether the first day is the second day or earlier.
GIVEN `the first` IS A DATE, `the second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day` `the first` `is on or before` `the second` IF
    DATE_SERIAL `the first` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `the second`

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a leap year` y IF
        (y MODULO 4 EQUALS 0)
    AND (    (NOT (y MODULO 100 EQUALS 0))
         OR  (y MODULO 400 EQUALS 0))

GIVEN m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of days in month` m `of` y MEANS
    BRANCH IF m EQUALS 2 THEN IF `is a leap year` y THEN 29 ELSE 28
           IF m EQUALS 4 THEN 30
           IF m EQUALS 6 THEN 30
           IF m EQUALS 9 THEN 30
           IF m EQUALS 11 THEN 30
           OTHERWISE 31

-- The same day of the month, n calendar years later (the last day of February where the start is 29 February and the
-- year is common).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the same day` n `years after` `the start` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY `the day of the month` (DATE_MONTH `the start`) `the new year`
    WHERE
        `the new year` MEANS DATE_YEAR `the start` PLUS n
        `the day of the month` MEANS
            IF DATE_DAY `the start` GREATER THAN `the number of days in month` (DATE_MONTH `the start`) `of` `the new year`
            THEN `the number of days in month` (DATE_MONTH `the start`) `of` `the new year`
            ELSE DATE_DAY `the start`

-- The day a given number of weeks after a day.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `weeks after` `the start` MEANS `the date` (n TIMES 7) `days after` `the start`
